# Data & state

There is no backend, API layer, or data-fetching library. State is React context + local component state.

## Library state
- `DoodleUIProvider` (`animations/DoodleUIProvider.tsx`): global `animate`, `forceAnimate`, `theme` ("light" | "dark" | "system"), `roughness`, `strokeWidth`, … Read via `useDoodleUI()` / `useAnimate(prop)` / `useSketchDefaults()`.
- `SketchSeedProvider` (`context/SketchSeedContext.tsx`, hook in `hooks/useSketchSeed.ts`): shared seed + `shuffle()`.
- Precedence everywhere: **explicit prop → provider → CSS variable → library constant**.
- Controlled/uncontrolled: Radix-backed components forward Radix `value`/`onValueChange`/`open`/`onOpenChange`; tested in `ControlledCompound.test.tsx`.
- Memoize context values with `useMemo` (perf audit fix — see `Table.tsx` `sketchContext`).

## Registry data flow
`scripts/build-registry.ts` reads `src/components/*.tsx` + JSDoc + `data/component-meta.ts` → writes `src/registry/data.ts`, root `registry.json` + `registry/*.json`, and `apps/docs/public/registry*`. Runs on every `build`.

## CLI (`src/cli`)
- `fetchRegistry()` GETs `DOODLEUI_REGISTRY_URL` or GitHub raw `master/registry.json` with a 4s abort, and silently falls back to the bundled `REGISTRY_DATA`:

```ts
  } catch {
    // Network or parse failure: fallback to bundled registry
  }
  return REGISTRY_DATA;
```
- Commands catch at the top level: `console.error("\nAdd error:", err?.message || err); process.exit(1);`.

## MCP (`src/mcp`)
- Tools read embedded data only (no network): registry, `theming.json`, `conventions.json`.
- Application errors return `structuredErrorResult(code, message, { suggestions })` as JSON text (no protocol `isError`), with Levenshtein-based name suggestions.

## Docs app
- Static export: no API routes, no runtime server. Build-time `fs` reads are allowed in server components (e.g. `app/blocks/page.tsx` reads block source files).
- Theme persisted in `localStorage` keys `doodle-ui-component-theme` / `doodle-ui-site-theme`.
